<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Hardware specifications for running local models</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The experiments with local models were conducted using a local HPC system, serving the LLMs with the following GPU hardware specifications:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">gpt-oss-120b</span>: 1x H100</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama 3.3 70b</span>: 4x A100</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama 4 Scout</span>: 4x H100</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DeepSeek-R1</span>: 8x H100</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Teuken 7b Instruct</span>: 1x A100</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Plots and results of the ensembling for released KBs</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Figures <a href="#A6.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix F Plots and results of the ensembling for released KBs ‣ Foundations of LLM Knowledge Materialization:Termination, Reproducibility, Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, <a href="#A6.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix F Plots and results of the ensembling for released KBs ‣ Foundations of LLM Knowledge Materialization:Termination, Reproducibility, Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and <a href="#A6.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix F Plots and results of the ensembling for released KBs ‣ Foundations of LLM Knowledge Materialization:Termination, Reproducibility, Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> we report the plots of triples shared across X of each topic’s base setting runs against different numbers of <span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">k</span>. Each plot shows the “elbow point” equals 3. The elbow method is a heuristic which involves plotting a variable (the number of shared triples) against <span id="A6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">k</span> and selecting the point farthest from a straight line drawn between the two extreme points in the plot (i.e. where the curve drops sharply, forming an “elbow” in the curve). Furthermore, in Table <a href="#A6.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix F Plots and results of the ensembling for released KBs ‣ Foundations of LLM Knowledge Materialization:Termination, Reproducibility, Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, we report the actual number of triples at different <span id="A6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">k</span> values. In bold the elbow point.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06780v1/elbow_babylon.png" id="A6.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/338;" width="476" height="338" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Triples shared across X runs of babylonGPTKB with different k values.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06780v1/elbow_tbbt.png" id="A6.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/338;" width="476" height="338" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Triples shared across X runs of tbbtGPTKB with different k values.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06780v1/elbow_dax40.png" id="A6.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/338;" width="476" height="338" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Triples shared across X runs of dax40GPTKB with different k values.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.T10" class="ltx_table">
